  "$comment": "Budgets for @tanrei/web, held by test/bundle-budget.test.mjs (bundles: bytes, gzip -9) and src/perf-budget.test.ts (runtime: counts, in Chromium). Each budget is the value measured when it was set and 5 %: for bytes rounded up to the next 100 bytes, for counts rounded down, so a count under 20 has no slack (one more update or one more unshared sheet is the regression itself). A byte size and a count are the same on every machine, so the margin absorbs growth that is worth its cost, never noise; the date and the load are recorded so a later measurement can be compared with this one. Over a budget is a finding: make the component cheaper, or raise its budget in the same change and say why in the changeset. A count that falls takes its budget down with it. bundles[*].measured is rewritten by TANREI_MEASURE_BUDGETS=1 node --test test/bundle-budget.test.mjs; a budget only by hand.",
